{"id":"w453-C0041-L1","status":"proved special case","kind":"conditional-clock-lemma","statement":"For any nearest-neighbor walk on Z^d with omega(x,e)>=kappa>0, any random time T in N union {infinity}, and R_T=sup_{n<=T}||X_n||_infinity, P(T>t)<=P(R_T>r)+(1-kappa^(r+1))^floor(t/(r+1)) for all integers r,t>=0, quenched and annealed.","assumptions":["d>=1","start at 0","nearest-neighbor transitions","0<kappa<=1/(2d)","uniform transition lower bound"],"source":{"type":"owner-own-work","path":"~/brain_workers/w453/LEMMAS.md","locator":"L1"},"proof_or_counterexample":"A deterministic outward path exits the box in <=r+1 steps with conditional probability >=kappa^(r+1); iterate conditional expectations at deterministic blocks, then use {T>t,R_T<=r} subset {sigma_r>t}. No stopping property or independence of T is used.","independent_reviewer":"w455 (pending)","remaining_gap":"No gap in the elementary inequality is identified; independent review pending. It does not control the range-tail term."}
{"id":"w453-C0041-L2","status":"proved special case","kind":"conditional-integrability-lemma","statement":"In L1's setting, if P(R_T>r)<=C exp(-lambda r) for all integer r>=0 with C finite and lambda>log(1/kappa), then E[T]<infinity.","assumptions":["all L1 assumptions","exponential spatial tail with lambda>log(1/kappa) under the same probability law"],"source":{"type":"owner-own-work","path":"~/brain_workers/w453/LEMMAS.md","locator":"L2"},"proof_or_counterexample":"Choose 1/lambda<a<1/log(1/kappa), set r=floor(a log(t+1)), and sum L1's polynomial range tail and stretched exponential box tail by Tonelli.","independent_reviewer":"w455 (pending)","remaining_gap":"C0041 supplies no such spatial-tail estimate; derivation from its exact assumptions is unproved. The condition is sufficient, not claimed necessary."}
